@startuml application-flow
!pragma layout smetana
title A1. Application Overview - Read Steps 1 to 6
left to right direction
skinparam componentStyle rectangle
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam ArrowColor #334155
skinparam defaultFontName SansSerif
skinparam packageStyle rectangle

actor "Visitor / Customer" as customer
actor "Administrator" as admin

node "Frontend container" #E0F2FE {
  component "Nginx\nStatic assets + SPA route fallback\n/api/* reverse proxy" as nginx
}

node "Browser" #E0F2FE {
  component "React application\nCoffee board: /\nSign in: /login\nRegistration: /register\nPersonal orders: /orders\nAdmin workspace: /admin" as react
  artifact "Bundled coffee photos\nBrand mark and favicon" as assets
}

node "Spring Boot backend container :18080" #DCFCE7 {
  component "Spring Security\nSession authentication + CSRF\nADMIN checks on catalog writes\nand /api/v1/admin/orders" as security
  component "HTTP controllers\n/api/v1/auth/*\n/api/v1/coffees\n/api/v1/orders\n/api/v1/admin/orders" as controllers
  component "Application services\nAccounts | Catalog | Orders\nPrice calculation and ownership" as services
  component "Spring Data JPA\nRepositories" as repositories
  component "Flyway\nVersioned schema migrations" as flyway
}

database "PostgreSQL\nCatalog | Accounts | Orders" as postgres #FEF3C7

customer --> react : 1. Browse, sign in, order
admin --> react : 1. Same login; role selects workspace
nginx --> react : 2. Deliver application
assets --> react : Bundled images
react --> nginx : 3. /api requests + session / CSRF
nginx --> security : 4. Proxy to backend:18080
security --> controllers : 5. Authenticate and authorize
controllers --> services : Dispatch validated request
services --> repositories : Apply business rules
repositories --> postgres : 6. Read / persist data
flyway ..> postgres : Startup only: migrate schema

note bottom of security
  Product reads are public; ordering requires authentication.
  Customers only receive their own order history.
  Admins can edit the catalog and list all orders.
  Hiding frontend controls is not the security boundary.
end note

note bottom of postgres
  Current runtime: local Docker Compose.
  Browser URL: http://localhost:8088
  PostgreSQL data persists in a named volume.
  Known demo accounts are seeded only by the dev profile.
  Sessions currently live in backend memory, not a shared store.
end note

legend bottom
  |= Color |= Responsibility |
  |<#E0F2FE> Blue | Browser and frontend delivery |
  |<#DCFCE7> Green | API security and business logic |
  |<#FEF3C7> Amber | Persistent data |
  Responses return along the request path.
  See A2 for numbered sign-in and order interactions.
  Keycloak, image uploads and cluster deployment remain planned.
endlegend
@enduml